From: Runeon Contributors <dev@runeon.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Keep NGX route files out of unrouted processes.

The d3dmetal-metalfx and dxmt-metalfx routes point the machine-wide NGX
registry value FullPath at a launcher directory. That value outlives
the routed process, so another process in the same session that looks
for NGX may read it and load the launcher's nvngx or _nvngx by full
path, although it was not given a MetalFX route.

After the route is settled, a process that did not end up on a MetalFX
route gets an exact-path disabled load order for nvngx and _nvngx in
each directory the launcher named in RUNEON_METALFX_NGX_PATH (only with
RUNEON_GFX_DIR_METALFX, as that route requires) and
RUNEON_DXMT_NGX_PATH. A MetalFX route that fell back because its
configuration is invalid counts as not routed.

Load order lookup tries the full path first, ignoring case and the NT
prefix, and the loader refuses a disabled module before mapping it. The
basename rules for nvngx and nvapi64, a program's own copies, the
System32 placeholder and launches without these variables are not
affected. The registry is neither read nor written here.

The load order parser splits on spaces and commas and stops at an
equals sign, so a directory containing one is ignored rather than
turned into rules for other modules.

--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/loadorder.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/loadorder.c
@@ -537,6 +537,33 @@
     setenv( dxmt_metalfx_vars[1], ngx, 1 );
     TRACE( GRAPHICS_ROUTES_DXMT_METALFX ": ngx %s\n", debugstr_a(ngx) );
     return TRUE;
+}
+
+
+/***************************************************************************
+ *	disable_ngx_files
+ *
+ * Runeon: refuse to load the launcher's NGX core files from this directory.
+ * Only these exact paths are disabled, so nvngx elsewhere keeps its load order.
+ * A path holding a load order separator could name other modules; it is
+ * ignored, which leaves its files loadable, and a launcher must not use one.
+ */
+static void disable_ngx_files( const char *ngx )
+{
+    static const char * const files[] = { "\\nvngx=", "\\_nvngx=" };
+    WCHAR entry[129 + sizeof("\\_nvngx=")];
+    unsigned int i, len, pos;
+    const char *p;
+
+    if (!is_ngx_path( ngx ) || strpbrk( ngx, " ,=" )) return;
+    for (len = 0; ngx[len]; len++) entry[len] = (unsigned char)ngx[len];
+    for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(files); i++)
+    {
+        pos = len;
+        for (p = files[i]; *p; p++) entry[pos++] = *p;
+        entry[pos] = 0;
+        add_load_order_override( entry );
+    }
 }
 
 
@@ -662,6 +689,13 @@
         for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(metalfx_vars); i++) unsetenv( metalfx_vars[i] );
     if (chosen != GRAPHICS_DXMT_METALFX && getenv( "RUNEON_DXMT_NGX_PATH" ))
         for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(dxmt_metalfx_vars); i++) unsetenv( dxmt_metalfx_vars[i] );
+    /* NGX finds its core through a machine-wide registry value, which a routed
+     * process may have left pointing at the launcher's files. */
+    if (chosen != GRAPHICS_D3DMETAL_METALFX && chosen != GRAPHICS_DXMT_METALFX)
+    {
+        if (getenv( "RUNEON_GFX_DIR_METALFX" )) disable_ngx_files( getenv( "RUNEON_METALFX_NGX_PATH" ) );
+        disable_ngx_files( getenv( "RUNEON_DXMT_NGX_PATH" ) );
+    }
 }
 
 
